{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 7, "model_name": "stockmark/stockmark-2-100b-instruct", "content": "Fair traveller, lend thine ear, for I shall weave a journey through the land of the rising sun, in a style most eloquent, most akin to the bard of Avon.\n\nOn the morn of thy sojourn, venture forth to the city of Tokyo, where thou shalt behold the might of the Shard-like Tokyo Skytree, piercing the heavens. There, peruse the treasures within the Tokyo National Museum, and later, in the evening, let thy feet dance upon the neon-lit paths of Shinjuku, where the night doth come alive with the cries of commerce and merriment.\n\nDoth thy spirit yearn for the ancients, then on the second morn, take thee to the sacred heart of Kyoto. There, in the embrace of nature, stand in awe before the ethereal beauty of Kinkaku-ji, the Golden Pavilion, where gold and nature doth conspire to dazzle the senses. Wander through the Ryoan-ji, the Temple of the Dragon at Peace, where the enigmatic rock garden shall stir thy soul.\n\nShould the call of the mountains be strong, on the third day, ascend to the tranquil heights of Hakone. Bathe in the restorative waters of its hot springs, and glimpse the majestic visage of Mount Fuji, standing sentinel over the land, a symbol of enduring beauty.\n\nAs thy journey draweth to its close, return to Tokyo, and let thy taste buds be tantalized by the delectable offerings of the Tsukiji Outer Market, a cornucopia of culinary delights. And in the twilight, as the sun doth bid farewell, stroll through the Meiji Shrine, where the modern and the ancient embrace in a dance of shadows and light.\n\nThus, fair traveller, with this itinerary, may thy footsteps be blessed, and thy memories be as timeless as the tales of Shakespeare.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Fair", "logprob": -2.766125440597534}, {"token": " trav", "logprob": -0.8085389137268066}, {"token": "eller", "logprob": -0.0010963627137243748}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.01193